      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00175:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "The Dienophile"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00001",
          "segmentId": "m00175:para:para-00001"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00001",
          "class": "scaled-down unnumbered",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00175:alt:fig-00001-alt",
              "text": "The structures and names of some Diels–Alder dienophiles. Ethylene: unreactive, propenal (acrolein), ethyl propenoate (ethyl acrylate), maleic anhydride, benzoquinone, propenenitrile (acrylonitrile), and methyl propynoate."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_14_05_001.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00002",
          "segmentId": "m00175:para:para-00002"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00002",
          "class": "scaled-down",
          "caption": {
            "segmentId": "m00175:caption:fig-00002-caption"
          },
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00175:alt:fig-00002-alt",
              "text": "Electrostatic potential maps along with the ball-and-stick models of ethylene, propenal, and propenenitrile each with an arrow pointing toward carbon-carbon double bonds."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_14_05_002.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00003",
          "segmentId": "m00175:para:para-00003"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00003",
          "class": "scaled-down unnumbered",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00175:alt:fig-00003-alt",
              "text": "The first reaction shows 1,3-butadiene reacting with methyl (Z)-2-butenoate to yield a cis product. The second reaction shows 1,3-butadiene reacting with methyl (E)-2-butenoate to yield trans product."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_14_05_003.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00004",
          "segmentId": "m00175:para:para-00004"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00004",
          "class": "scaled-down unnumbered",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00175:alt:fig-00004-alt",
              "text": "A 7-membered bicyclic ring with C 2 bonded to an axial R group (endo) and an equatorial R group (exo).. To the right, the ball-and-stick model of 7-membered bicyclic ring is depicted."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_14_05_004.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00005",
          "segmentId": "m00175:para:para-00005"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00005",
          "class": "scaled-down unnumbered",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00175:alt:fig-00005-alt",
              "text": "A reaction shows 1,3-cyclopentadiene reacting with maleic anhydride to form endo product. Exo product is not formed."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_14_05_005.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
